<div class="guide-styles" data-ay-injected="true" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Phase 3 Best in Slot Gear list for Retribution Paladin DPS in Wrath of the Lich King Classic. Gear in this guide is primarily obtained from Trial of the Grand Crusader. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from raids, dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="best-in-slot">Best in Slot Gear for Retribution Paladin Phase 3</h2>
<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Hit - Aim for 8% Hit%, 263 rating, because all of your abilities are under some form of hit requirement.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Strength out the wazzoo - Everything you have scales with both ap and spell power, and strength gives you the most bang for your buck for that.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Crit /<wbr/> Agi - Your next prio stat, this is very strong as many of your abilities will proc <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=53382/righteous-vengeance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_righteousvengeance.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Righteous Vengeance</span></a>.  This is more important with your 2piece Tier 9 <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67188/item-paladin-t9-retribution-2p-bonus-righteous-vengeance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Item - Paladin T9 Retribution 2P Bonus (Righteous Vengeance)</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Expertise - after this point your expertise is the next thing to keep an eye on.  This is much lower value than hit because your Judgement, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48806/hammer-of-wrath">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_thunderclap.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Hammer of Wrath</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48801/exorcism">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_excorcism_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Exorcism</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48819/consecration">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_innerfire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Consecration</span></a> all ignore dodge possibilities, however with P3 &amp; 4 its a higher priority.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Haste - This is still decent but not nearly as good as it was in TBC.  This will have some issues where <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48801/exorcism">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_excorcism_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Exorcism</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=48819/consecration">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_innerfire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Consecration</span></a> will have their GCD reduced, which will cause weird stutters in your rotation.  These shouldn't be a major concern but its something to note.</div></li></ol>While all of these stat priorities are important, what really comes down to it is these 3 steps:<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">The Two Piece Tier 9 <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=67188/item-paladin-t9-retribution-2p-bonus-righteous-vengeance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Item - Paladin T9 Retribution 2P Bonus (Righteous Vengeance)</span></a> is CRITICAL to get as soon as possible.  This is worth getting even if you have to result with 245 pieces that eventually get upgraded to 258.  It should be noted that while the 4p is "good" its not nearly impactful and it forces you into some weird stat setups, which makes things less ideal.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Maintain 8% hit, 263 rating.  This is your highest priority thing to not go too far over and waste the stat, but also not to go more than 1-3 hit under cap.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Avoid Armor Penetration: well over half of your damage is holy damage, which completely ignores armor.  This is the only stat to avoid</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Along this line, expertise is not nearly as valuable for ret in wotlk, 35-45% of your damage (depending on fight /<wbr/> glyphs) will avoid the dodge roll.  It is a higher value stat than in P1 and P2, but its still not a mandatory thing to cap.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Acquire Item level with a focus on sockets.  All other stats are "Decent" with strength being obviously the best, hence the sockets.  However agi leather gear often times outperforms the strength plate gear as item budgets for a stat become more expensive as you have more of a stat.  Leather gear often times have an extra stat to spread the item budget across, making it have more effective stats on it than the plate gear.  You shouldn't focus on one or the other, when in doubt run things through wowsims to verify, but in general an item level upgrade that doesn't have armp and doesn't throw off your hit rating is an overall upgrade.</div></li></ol>In P3, we are looking at two primary setups that have only a gemming change between horde and alliance (although the names of the items will be different between the two setups):<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">An absolute BIS Setup.  This will assume your guild will give you access to a full 258 setup.  NOTE: Dwarfs should continue to use <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45599/sabatons-of-lifeless-night">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sabatons of Lifeless Night</span></a> as they get enough expertise from being dwarves that these end up being better than the TOTGC boots.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">An "ideal" setup that actually focuses on filling most of the slots with Ulduar gear &amp; avoids high competition items from P3.  These sets are &lt; 4% total DPS from being in a "Full BIS" state so they are a great place to aim to get.  These sets may not be completely optimal in their respective vacuum, but focus on a setup that doesn't waste any items going then into "Full BIS"</div></li></ol>NOTE that none of these sets will use <a class="q1 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=43869/glyph-of-seal-of-vengeance">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glyph_majorpaladin.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Glyph of Seal of Vengeance</span></a> as they have plenty of expertise without it.<div class="clear"></div>
