<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="p2-gear-for-p3">Strong P2 gear for going into P3</h3>A small thing to touch on is noting any gear from Ulduar that will be useful in and throughout P3.  For the retribution paladin, we will not have any items from P2 that are BIS in P3, however we will have a number of items that will come "close" to their P3 counterpart and will be used at least until the heroic (258) versions are acquired:<ul>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45663/armbands-of-bedlam">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_bracer_23a.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Armbands of Bedlam</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=46095/soul-devouring-cinch">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_belt_37c.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul-Devouring Cinch</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45599/sabatons-of-lifeless-night">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sabatons of Lifeless Night</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45473/embrace-of-the-gladiator">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_leather_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Embrace of the Gladiator</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45472/warhelm-of-the-champion">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_134.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warhelm of the Champion</span></a></div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45134/plated-leggings-of-ruination">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_25.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Plated Leggings of Ruination</span></a></div></li></ul>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="p3-gear-for-p4">Strong P3 gear for going into P4</h3>Much like in ulduar, there are some pieces of gear from P3 that you will be using well into P4 progression and gearing, and its pretty important to make sure you grab those.<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Two Piece 258 T9 using Shoulders /<wbr/> Gloves.  Running 2p/<wbr/>2p early in P4 will be optimal until you can deck out in full 277, and you will want to use shoulders /<wbr/> gloves from this tier since they have the lowest item budget loss for lower ilvl items.  These require 2 <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47557/regalia-of-the-grand-conqueror">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_chain_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Regalia of the Grand Conqueror</span></a> total to get, and these should be your first 258 tier items that you get.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_horde.gif");'></span>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47464/deaths-choice">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death's Choice</span></a> <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_alliance.gif");'></span>[/<wbr/>icon]<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47131/deaths-verdict">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_bone_skull_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Death's Verdict</span></a> going to be your BIS trinket for the rest of the game, so you absolutely want to get a 258 DC /<wbr/> DV</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">You want to get the axe <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_alliance.gif");'></span> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47078/justicebringer">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_103.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Justicebringer</span></a> /<wbr/> <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/side_horde.gif");'></span> <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=47446/dual-blade-butcher">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_106.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dual-blade Butcher</span></a> from TOTGC for your linear progression into <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49888/shadows-edge">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_113.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shadow's Edge</span></a> and eventually into <a class="q5 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49623/shadowmourne">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_axe_113.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shadowmourne</span></a>.</div></li></ol>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="gemming">Gemming your Gear</h3>When gemming your gear you want to keep in mind a few basic notes:<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Jewelcrafting is BIS for you, but by only 2 total strength when compared to blacksmithing .  This will give you a bonus of 42 to what ever stats you gem, where as blacksmithing will give you only 40.  With this you will want to make sure you are always running 3 <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=42225/dragons-eye">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_dragonseye01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dragon's Eye</span></a> gems.  These can be purchased with your <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/currency=61/dalaran-jewelcrafters-token">
<span>
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_variety_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Dalaran Jewelcrafter's Token</span></span></a>.  Ideally these should all be <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=42142/bold-dragons-eye">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_dragonseye05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bold Dragon's Eye</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Never be afraid to gem for hit. <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=42156/rigid-dragons-eye">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_dragonseye03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rigid Dragon's Eye</span></a> will provide about 1% hit, <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40125/rigid-kings-amber">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_38.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rigid King's Amber</span></a> provides about .61% hit, and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40143/etched-ametrine">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_39.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Etched Ametrine</span></a> will provide ~.3% hit.  These are great ways to make up for a few points missing in a great gear setup otherwise, and are used in the P3 Horde BIS setup.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Because you want to be running <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=41398/relentless-earthsiege-diamond">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_shadowspirit_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relentless Earthsiege Diamond</span></a>, you will only ever need one blue gem, which you should supply by using a single <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=49110/nightmare-tear">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_pearl_12.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nightmare Tear</span></a>.  This gem provides more overall stats than any purple gem you could use.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">Almost all other gems will be <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40111/bold-cardinal-ruby">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_37.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bold Cardinal Ruby</span></a>.  The only time you should deviate from this after hit cap is if you can get a yellow socket with 4 strength per yellow socket bonus.  If that's the case you can fill it with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=40142/inscribed-ametrine">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelcrafting_gem_39.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscribed Ametrine</span></a>. This <i>may</i> appear to sim slightly lower than just str, but it will improve your overall consistency going into this phase.</div></li></ol>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="gearing-in-totgc">Gearing in TOTGC</h3>With TOTGC for ret, the main go to gearing idea is going to be 258 &gt; Ulduar Hardmodes (252) &gt; 245 gear (either 25 or 10man heroic).  There are 0 items from 10man that are on your BIS list, so its best to just focus all your energy into the 25 man gear.  Its also noted that there's only 6 items total needed to get you to 4% of your power level for the tier: Libram, 2p Tier, trinket, weapon and 272 cape; so plan your upgrades appropriately.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="body-armor">Body Armor for Retribution Paladin Phase 3</h2>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="head">Head for Retribution Paladin Phase 3</h3>Your end goal is to get <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=48619/liadrins-helm-of-triumph">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_98.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Liadrin's Helm of Triumph</span></a>, however <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45472/warhelm-of-the-champion">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_134.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Warhelm of the Champion</span></a> will tide your over for a LONG time until then.  You won't want to swap over until you have a hit piece to compensate, typically its the bracers slot which is very competitive.  <br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Helm Enchant</b>: <a class="q7 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=50367/arcanum-of-torment">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_rampage.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Arcanum of Torment</span></a>, requires Revered reputation with <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/faction=1098/knights-of-the-ebon-blade">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Knights of the Ebon Blade</span></a>.<div class="pad"></div>
