<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="weapons">Weapons  for Retribution Paladin Phase 3</h2>
<div class="pad"></div>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="two-hand-weapons-for-retribution-paladin-phase-3">Two Hand Weapons for Retribution Paladin Phase 3</h4>Your choice of weapon comes down to Mace (expertise) vs Axe (armp).  The sets involved with each are both approximately equal, but the mace will be infinitely easier to get early on, so it will be the one recommended.  You really want to get this weapon asap as its about a 150 dps increase over <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/item=45516/voldrethar-dark-blade-of-oblivion">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_136.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Voldrethar, Dark Blade of Oblivion</span></a> and really helps with consistency from the expertise added.  Its not worth worrying about any other 2h from TOTGC, only axe /<wbr/> mace.  As a note you should eventually try to get an axe to set yourself up for the P4 progression set.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Weapon Enchants</b>: <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/wotlk/spell=59621/enchant-weapon-berserking">
